  "subject": "a young couple climbing the stone stairs to a hillside temple in the dark before sunrise, she counting steps out loud and he carrying a thermos of hot ginger tea, reaching the top just as the bell rings",
  "caption": "Taiwanese Hokkien hapa haole Hawaiian swing, 1950s lounge style. Lap steel guitar with gentle sliding glissandos; ukulele soft strum; walking upright bass; brushed snare in a relaxed swing. Warm tape room tone, intimate and uncluttered. A soft male baritone, close-mic, shy and sincere. 84 BPM, G major. Warm, shy, tender. No electric drums, no autotune, no pop-ballad strings, no rock guitar, no reggae skank.",
  "lyrics": "[Verse]\n四點半 天猶未光\n你佇樓跤 等我落來\n手電仔照 石階一坎\n你講欲算 到廟埕\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n一坎 兩坎 你算出聲\n我揹一罐 燒薑母茶\n\n[Chorus]\n天光進前 陪你行山\n石階冷冷 你手燒燒\n算毋著 嘛無要緊\n閣算一擺 我陪你\n\n[Verse]\n半山腰 你喘袂離\n坐佇石頭 歇一下\n我倒茶 吹予冷\n你講薑 傷過辣\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n樹頂鳥仔 先叫一聲\n山跤路燈 一葩一葩化\n\n[Chorus]\n天光進前 陪你行山\n你行頭前 我行後壁\n算到三百 你越頭笑\n講我跤步 傷慢矣\n\n[Verse]\n廟埕到位 鐘拄好摃\n日頭對海 爬起來\n你頭毛 予風吹亂\n我毋敢 共你講\n\n[Bridge]\n三百外坎 我無算著\n干焦算 你笑幾擺\n\n[Chorus]\n天光進前 陪你行山\n明年今仔日 閣來行\n石階猶原 冷冷冷\n你的手 我牽牢牢\n\n[Outro]\n一坎 兩坎\n天光矣",
